   "The ECB hiked rates by 25bp to 2.50% in September, with the policy statement signaling a shift toward a more forceful response to persistent inflation.",
   "Deutsche Bank maintains its call for a terminal rate of 2.75% in December, noting that the onus is on data to weaken quickly to prevent further hikes.",
   "Core inflation is projected to remain 30bp above target at the end of the forecast horizon, justifying the hawkish bias.",
   "President Lagarde's press conference tone was more ambiguous than the policy statement, as she avoided endorsing market pricing and emphasized a data-dependent, meeting-by-meeting approach.",
   "The ECB upgraded its 2026 and 2027 GDP growth projections, citing stronger private consumption and a resilient labor market.",
   "Risks to the terminal rate are two-sided: while high energy prices could trigger demand destruction, resilient growth and elevated energy costs might push rates to 3%+.",
