  "insights": [
   "Goldman Sachs introduces a new Permian Basin natural gas processing capacity model, forecasting a ~6% volume CAGR (wet gas) from 2025-2032.",
   "The basin requires at least ~11.5 bcf/d of new processing capacity by 2032, with ~14 bcf/d likely needed to maintain current utilization rates.",
   "Processing capacity is not expected to constrain overall supply growth, unlike potential bottlenecks in long-haul gas pipelines, compression, and water disposal.",
   "Targa Resources (TRGP) is the top pick to gain market share, projected to reach ~27% share by 2032 from ~23% currently, driven by organic wins like the XOM agreement.",
   "Kinetik Holdings (KNTK) is identified as the most likely M&A takeout target within the coverage universe due to its footprint and NGL feedstock potential.",
   "Midstream operators are increasingly focused on 'sour' gas capabilities (H2S/CO2 treatment), with EPD, TRGP, and KNTK investing in specialized infrastructure.",
   "Public midstream operators now represent ~90% of total Permian processing capacity, up from 73% in 2019, following significant consolidation.",
   "OKE's pending acquisition of Brazos Midstream is highlighted as a key example of ongoing consolidation to feed integrated downstream NGL systems.",
