   "Stabilizing the debt-to-GDP ratio requires balancing the primary budget outside of recessions, which would require a large 3pp deficit reduction.",
   "The US government collects less revenue as a share of GDP than the G7 average, suggesting potential room for revenue increases.",
   "A larger productivity boost from AI could slow the rise in debt-to-GDP but is unlikely to eliminate the need for fiscal consolidation.",
   "The risk of a classic debt crisis is low due to the US issuing debt in dollars and setting its own monetary policy, but fiscal inaction risks pressure on the Fed to keep rates too low, potentially fueling inflation.",
